{
  "comment": "PHYS variant (current Stage-1 recipe): env myoAssistLegImitationExoOSLPhys-v0 = hard ankle limit + OSL motor model (peak 145.25 Nm, 6.13 rad/s, assumed reflected inertia 0.1; src/terrain_memory_prosthesis/envs/osl_physics.py) and the SAME ground type as Stage 2: a 100 m heightfield with 1e-5 m relief (cells 25 cm), because a plane-trained gait fell on every heightfield even at 0.01 mm relief (pilot 06). | P1 x C1 (proprioception only, feed-forward MLP): myolegs22 + OpenSourceLeg_A_L1 (right transtibial powered-ankle prosthesis), flat terrain. Obs layout (40): qpos[0:8] qvel[8:17] muscle_act[17:35] sensor[35:39]=(r_foot,l_foot,r_toes,l_toes) target_vel[39]. Action layout (19): 18 muscles + 1 prosthesis ankle torque (osl_ankle_torque_actuator, idx 18). exo_actor = prosthesis controller; P1 input = joint angles, joint velocities, foot contacts, target velocity (muscle activations excluded: a prosthesis cannot measure them). No terrain information. P2 will append the terrain-preview channels to this block. evaluate_frequency is set very high on purpose: the in-training analyzer hung in a headless test run (cause not found). Run: MUJOCO_GL=egl python rl_train/run_train.py --config_file_path <this file> --config.env_params.num_envs <n_cpus> PPO recipe taken from a previous SDU project that trained walking with this framework for 30M steps (lr 1e-4, rollout buffer 16384 = num_envs*n_steps, minibatch 8192, 30 epochs, CPU only; ~10.5 h on 64 CPUs with 128 envs). Keep num_envs*n_steps = 16384: e.g. 128 envs x 128 steps, 64 x 256, 32 x 512.",
